ecord on Richland County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids, January to February and August to September each came in under 90% of normal in 37 years. In 2025, November to December came in at 51% of normal and August to September at 62%. Every grid had its driest year in 1953, with grid 22367 at 61%.</p>"}
